  data: {
    LLM: "Start with hands that play well both ways (e.g., A-K-Q-J-10 double suited). Don't draw blindly for a flush if it ruins your Omaha hand. The 'One Open' card gives info to everyoneâ€”if you draw an Ace face-up, everyone knows you have it.\n\nScooping: You need to win both halves. If you have the Nut Flush in Omaha, and a Pair in hand, you might win half. But Quads in hand and nothing in Omaha is also half. Aim for both.\n\nBlockers: Since you see discarded/open cards, use that info. If an opponent draws 1 card and gets a King face-up, you know one King is gone.",
